Install duolog for me. duolog lets Claude Code and Codex hand work to each
other. This works on macOS, Linux and Windows.

Step 1. Before you change anything, ask me one question, exactly as written
below. FOLDER is the absolute path of the folder that duolog sets up: the top
folder of the Git repository you are in (for a linked worktree, its main
checkout), or the current directory outside Git. Do not reword the question,
do not add choices or a recommendation, and do not ask anything else first.

The question: Install duolog into this project folder: FOLDER?
Choice 1: Yes, install here. Set up duolog for this project in FOLDER.
Choice 2: Skip. Do not install into this folder. Finish the rest of the
install.

If you have a question tool with options, such as AskUserQuestion in Claude
Code, call it once: the question above, the header Project, the two choices
as two options, one answer only. Any answer other than choice 1 means choice
2.

If you have no question tool, as in Codex, print exactly these four lines,
then stop and wait for my reply:
Install duolog into this project folder: FOLDER?
  1. Yes, install here
  2. Skip
Reply with 1 or 2.
Accept only 1 or 2. On any other reply, print the same four lines again.

On choice 2, do steps 2 and 3 only, so FOLDER stays unchanged, and say that
duolog install --scope project sets up a project later.

Step 2. Install the duolog binary with one command for this system:
  macOS, Linux or WSL: curl -fsSL https://github.com/{{.Owner}}/{{.Repo}}/releases/{{$from}}/install.sh | sh
  Windows PowerShell: irm https://github.com/{{.Owner}}/{{.Repo}}/releases/{{$from}}/install.ps1 | iex
Then run: duolog version
If the shell cannot find duolog, use the full path that the installer
printed.

Step 3. Add the duolog plugin to the agent you are:
  Claude Code: claude plugin marketplace add {{.Owner}}/{{.Repo}}
  then:        claude plugin install duolog@duolog
  Codex:       codex plugin marketplace add {{.Owner}}/{{.Repo}}
  then:        codex plugin add duolog@duolog

Step 4. In FOLDER, run: duolog install --scope project

Step 5. Run: duolog doctor
Then tell me in at most five short lines what is done and what I must do
myself, such as approving the hooks in /hooks in Codex, or starting a new
session so that the hooks load.

Rules: run each command yourself. Stop at the first command that fails and
show me its error. Do not edit any other file. Do not answer permission
prompts for me.
